  "details": "For the uninitiated: https://docs.vrchat.com/v2018.4.4/docs/avatar-performance-ranking-system\n\nUnless I am reading the new performance system documentation wrong it seems like it will use your lowest ranking to be chosen as the rank that gets displayed for your avatar. This means that even if you pass all performance checks and you have an avatar that is 50,001 polys that avatar is ranked as poor. \n\nAn avatar like that should not be ranked the same as an avatar that has a poor performance rank in all fields. I'm assuming that the avatar ranking is to let the unaware know about unoptimized avatars, but some people (new users especially) may just look at the rank and not the avatar's details and just assume a person's avatar is unoptimized and block. \n\nI think a better system would be to have the average of all of the rankings displayed instead of the lowest.  So the avatar in the above example would be a very good instead of a poor.",
